  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Labour Organization (ILO) is set to conduct training sessions on International Labour Standards (ILS). These sessions are designed to enhance awareness about these standards and build the capabilities of national stakeholders from the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development (MHRSD), judicial bodies, and other relevant stakeholders. This will offer guidance on their practical application to benefit everyone. Furthermore, these capacity-building efforts will serve to deepen the participants&#x2019; comprehension of the ILO&#x2019;s role, the ILS framework, and the operations of the ILO&#x2019;s supervisory entities. These entities are responsible for overseeing the enactment of ILO conventions and recommendations, as well as evaluating the alignment of domestic laws and practices with global labour norms. The educational programs will also acquaint attendees with best practices from around the world to support the implementation of ILS, with a particular focus on the ILO fundamental conventions.</narrative>
  </description>
